1)d. Write a HTML program, in such a way that, rather than placing large images on a page, the
preferred technique is to use thumbnails by setting the height and width parameters to something
like to 100*100 pixels.Each thumbnail image is also a link to a full sized version of the image. Create
an image gallery using this technique .
<!DOCTYPE html>
<head>
<title>Image Gallery</title>
<style>
body {
display: flex;
gap: 10px;
justify-content: center;
padding: 20px;
}
img {
width: 100px;
height: 100px;
object-fit: cover;
border: 2px solid #ccc;
border-radius: 5px;
}
img:hover {
border-color: #555;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<a href="img1.jpg"><img src="images/thumb1.jpg" alt="Image 1"></a>
<a href="img2.jpg"><img src="images/thumb2.jpg" alt="Image 2"></a>
</body>
</html>
